    79	E: pooled g(C*) - g(C-thr12) > 0 under D2+H3, computed exactly from the paired per-seed values (not against a rounded
    80	threshold). Met if it holds under both base and doubled records; failed if it fails under both (a tie, exactly 0, is not
    81	met); not established if they disagree; "not available" if a record is missing or a value is nonfinite (reported
    82	separately, never a failure). No expectation on the category.
    83	
    84	## 5. Cost and spending controls
    85	
    86	`python3 docs/revision/followup2/cost_estimate.py`: 17.65 core-hours, 1.91 USD at the benchmark's 0.108 USD per
    87	core-hour; billed path on one 16-vCPU pod 3.56 hours (reproduction gate 0.61 h, searches, six serial reference calls,
    88	X7-SC evaluation and doubling, 0.3 h preparation and tail) = 1.99 USD at 0.56 USD per hour. Estimate 1.99 USD
    89	(x 1.25 = 2.49); **stop cap and reservation 3.00 USD**, the full allowance, in the ledger category `followup` (cap 22 USD
    90	shared by all follow-up runs: reset 5, churn 8, Run A 3, Run B 4.25, total 20.25; `budget_followup.py reserve`). A paid run
    91	requires `--started-at <allocation time>` and counts earlier failed attempts (`--prior-spend-usd`). The driver checks
    92	the cap between stages: a stage starts only if the billed time so far
    93	plus its estimate stays within the cap; a running stage is never killed (author's instruction); the run stops, writes
    94	`cost_stop.json` and an inventory, and reports. This is an admission limit, not a billing ceiling: a stage that starts
    95	within the cap finishes, and the pod is deleted after it.
    96	
    97	## 6. Steps
    98	
    99	1. Internal review to consensus; freeze this plan.
   100	2. Reserve 3.00 USD in the ledger; one pod: `reset_followup_v2.py --reproduce --require-identical`, then `runnerup_v2.py
   101	   --stage all --workers 12 --reset-mac M --reset-pod P --doubling-evidence D --cap-usd 3.00 --started-at T`; delete and verify the pod; record the spend.
   102	3. Analysis on the Mac from the retrieved records; a paper paragraph and table labelled exploratory, after review.

